  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Radius of Bohr&#39;s orbit is given as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>n = orbit number</p><p>Z = atomic number<br /><br />For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math> Bohr&#39;s orbit of <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>Li</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>2+</mtext></mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
